--unwind 6

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §12a. PLR: closures capture the loop variable's cell
(late binding), so every lambda created in the loop returns the final
value (fns[0]() == 2). CBMC captures the value at creation time, so it
returns 0 and the assertion fails. The KNOWNBUG regex states the
PLR-correct SUCCESSFUL. A faithful fix needs shared mutable cells for
captured free variables instead of value capture; it is a precision
gap (false positive, sound direction), not a missed bug.
